['You (New Joiner)', q{<strong>Shipped:</strong> spike merged; doc fix live; reconciliation view running on event timestamp. <strong>Next:</strong> sign-off walkthrough with Elena Wednesday; production-data access day four. <strong>Blocked:</strong> nothing — <em>the word "blocked" should be rare in my updates.</em>}, q{<strong>Shipped：</strong>spike 已合并；文档修复已上线；对账视图跑在事件时间戳上。<strong>Next：</strong>周三与 Elena 走查签批；生产数据权限第 4 天。<strong>Blocked：</strong>无——<em>"blocked" 一词在我的汇报里应该稀有。</em>}],
['You (New Joiner)', q{<strong>Risk, named honestly:</strong> the reactivation flag in source data is unreliable (race condition REF-2214) — <em>the dashboard is correct today; if the source job is patched, the timestamp join must be re-verified.</em> <strong>Ask:</strong> Daniel B — <em>ten minutes this week to confirm the re-verification step belongs in the pipeline ticket?</em>}, q{<strong>风险，诚实命名：</strong>源数据的再激活标志不可靠（竞态 REF-2214）——<em>仪表盘今天是对的；如果源作业将来被修复，时间戳连接需要复验。</em><strong>请求：</strong>Daniel B——<em>本周 10 分钟，确认复验步骤是否应写进管道工单？</em>}],
['Elena (Tech Lead)', q{Reading it as a manager would: <strong>ninety seconds, and I know the state of your week better than from any standup.</strong> The headline works — <em>"recommendation" is the word that makes it skimmable</em>; I read your conclusion, then decide if I need your reasons.}, q{以经理视角读了一遍：<strong>90 秒，比任何站会都清楚你这一周的状态。</strong>结论行成立——<em>"recommendation" 一词让它变得可速读</em>；我先读你的结论，再决定要不要看理由。}],
['Sarah (Manager)', q{And the risk section is <strong>the part that gets you trusted</strong> — you named the failure mode that has not happened yet, with the re-verification plan attached. <em>That is senior behaviour in week two.</em>}, q{风险段是<strong>赢得信任的部分</strong>——你命名了一个尚未发生的故障模式，并附上了复验计划。<em>这是第二周就很资深的标志。</em>}],
['Daniel B (Senior Dev)', q{The ask reached me as a <strong>ten-minute decision, not a mystery</strong> — yes, the re-verification step belongs in the pipeline ticket; I will add it. <em>Note for your next update: put the ask with a deadline — "by Wednesday" — and I would have answered it same-day.</em>}, q{这个请求到我这里是<strong>一个 10 分钟的决定，不是谜题</strong>——是的，复验步骤该进管道工单，我来加。<em>下次更新提示：给请求加期限——"周三前"——我当天就会答。</em>}],
['You (New Joiner)', q{Logged — <strong>every ask gets a deadline from now on.</strong> One habit I am taking from this: <em>the subject line is written last, and it is written as the update itself.</em> If the subject cannot carry the state, the email is too complicated.}, q{记下——<strong>从现在起每个请求都带期限。</strong>一个习惯：主题行最后写，而且写成汇报本身。<em>如果主题行装不下状态，说明邮件太复杂了。</em>}],
],
phrases => [
['Subject', q{Churn dashboard — on track for Thursday; one risk needs a yes/no.}, q{流失仪表盘——周四按期；一个风险需要是/否决定。}, q{Subject-as-update: state, date, and the decision needed. Inbox readers are done after the subject line.}],
['Headline', q{Recommendation: ship Thursday with the timestamp join; gap understood and documented.}, q{建议：周四带时间戳连接上线；偏差已查明并记录。}, q{"Recommendation" licenses skimming — the reader takes your conclusion or asks for your reasons, never both by default.}],
['Shipped', q{Spike merged; doc fix live; view running on timestamp.}, q{spike 已合并；文档修复已上线；视图跑在时间戳上。}, q{Past-participle inventory — merged, live, running: finished things, each with its evidence.}],
['Risk', q{The dashboard is correct today; if the source is patched, the join must be re-verified.}, q{仪表盘今天是对的；若源头被修复，连接需复验。}, q{The honest risk: correct now + the trigger that would break it + the plan. Three clauses, zero fear-mongering.}],
['Ask', q{Ten minutes this week to confirm X — by Wednesday?}, q{本周 10 分钟确认 X——周三前？}, q{Sized ask with deadline. Daniel B told you: the deadline is what converts an ask into a same-day answer.}],
],
vocab => [
['Status update', 'n. 进度汇报', 'The written pulse: shipped, next, blocked, risk, ask.'],
['Recommendation', 'n. 建议', 'Your conclusion, stated first — the word that makes updates skimmable.'],
['Sign-off', 'n. 签批', 'Formal approval to proceed; walkthroughs produce them.'],
['Risk', 'n. 风险', 'A named future failure mode with a plan attached — never a vague worry.'],
['Re-verification', 'n. 复验', 'Re-checking an assumption after its input changes — your dashboard\'s dependency.'],
['Race condition', 'n. 竞态条件', 'REF-2214\'s disease; the reason your join cannot trust the flag.'],
['Deadline', 'n. 期限', 'What turns an ask into a scheduled answer.'],
