grammar => [
['Past participles as shipped inventory', q{<em>"Spike merged; doc fix live; view running."</em> — past participles and adjectives as a completed-state inventory: merged, live, running. No "I have done X" needed — the participle IS the done. Status English is participle English; sentences with "I" in the shipped section read as activity, not outcome.}, q{"Spike merged; doc fix live; view running."——过去分词与形容词构成"已完成状态"清单：merged、live、running。不需要"I have done X"——分词本身就是完成。进度英语就是分词英语；shipped 段里出现"I"读起来是活动，不是成果。}],
['The today/then risk frame', q{<em>"The dashboard is correct today; if the source is patched, the join must be re-verified."</em> — present simple for the current state, first conditional for the trigger, modal for the consequence. Three clauses that price a risk honestly: true now, breaks when X, plan is Y. Vague risks say "there might be issues"; priced risks say this.}, q{"The dashboard is correct today; if the source is patched, the join must be re-verified."——现在时讲当前状态，第一类条件句讲触发器，情态动词讲后果。三个从句诚实定价一个风险：现在为真、X 时会坏、计划是 Y。模糊的风险说"可能有Issues"；定价的风险这么说。}],
],
tips => [
q{<strong>Write the subject last, as the update itself.</strong> If the subject carries state, date and decision-needed, many readers need nothing else.},
q{<strong>"Recommendation:" is the magic word.</strong> It converts your email from a story into a decision document.},
q{<strong>Keep "blocked" rare.</strong> An update whose blocked line is always full reads as a diary of helplessness. Flag dependencies as dependencies.},
q{<strong>Price the risk in three clauses.</strong> Correct today; breaks when X; plan is Y. That is the whole grammar of credible risk reporting.},
q{<strong>Every ask gets a deadline.</strong> Daniel B answered same-day because the ask had a date. The deadline is a gift to the busy.},
],
practice => [
{ t => 'Write yours', p => 'Draft your own five-line update this week: subject-as-update, recommendation headline, shipped/next/blocked, one priced risk, one sized ask with deadline.', a => q{Then test: read only the subject line and the recommendation — does a manager know your state and your ask? If yes, the remaining lines are evidence; if no, the headline is hiding the point.} },
{ t => 'Risk pricing', p => 'Price these vague risks in the three-clause frame: (a) "the data might have issues", (b) "the migration could be risky", (c) "performance may degrade".', a => q{(a) "Counts are correct today; if the source backfills, the totals shift — re-run due Friday." (b) "Migration is reversible today; after cutover the rollback window is 24h — decision point Thursday." (c) "P95 is 400ms now; beyond 5k concurrent users it degrades — load test booked Wednesday." Today/trigger/plan, every time.} },
{ t => 'Subject line gym', p => 'Write subject lines for three states: on track with a decision needed; at risk due to external dependency; shipped and closed.', a => q{Models: "Churn dashboard — on track Thursday; need yes/no on join approach." "Access ticket day 5 — pairing workaround active, but Thursday ship at risk if no reply." "Reconciliation view — shipped and verified; doc updated." State + date + decision, under twelve words.} },
],
},
