grammar => [
['Either/or boundary questions', q{<em>"Silent, or thinking-aloud welcome? My hands or yours?"</em> — compressed either/or questions get binary answers, which is what boundaries need. The full-sentence version ("would you prefer me to be silent?") invites softening; the compressed version invites a decision. Boundary questions live in the compressed register.}, q{"Silent, or thinking-aloud welcome? My hands or yours?"——压缩的 either/or 问句得到二元回答，而边界正需要二元回答。完整版（"你希望我保持沉默吗？"）招来客套；压缩版招来决定。边界问题属于压缩语域。}],
['Opinions with built-in discounts', q{<em>"That is a week-three opinion from someone who has never faced a CFO — I am holding it loosely."</em> — the grammar of priced opinions: [opinion] + [source discount]. It reads as senior because it does the reviewer\'s job in advance. Compare the unpriced version — "I would have cut slide six" — same content, no discount, invites defence instead of discussion.}, q{"That is a week-three opinion from someone who has never faced a CFO — I am holding it loosely."——带定价的观点语法：[观点] + [来源折扣]。它显得资深，因为它提前做了评审者的工作。对比未定价版："I would have cut slide six"——内容相同、没有折扣，招来辩护而非讨论。}],
