focus => 'Mandatory modules as domain education: what the rules mean for your daily English',
scenario => [
q{Week three. Your screen fills with <strong>mandatory compliance modules</strong>: data privacy, market conduct, anti-bribery. Twelve hours of clicks between you and production access. <strong>Most new joiners treat this as a toll booth; the smart ones treat it as a phrasebook.</strong>},
q{第三周。屏幕上挤满了<strong>强制合规课程</strong>：数据隐私、市场行为、反贿赂。你与生产环境权限之间隔着 12 小时的点击。<strong>多数新人把它当收费站；聪明人把它当 phrasebook（常用语手册）。</strong>},
q{Every compliance module is written in <strong>the regulator-facing English of the bank</strong> — and that register is exactly what your future emails, tickets and audits will use. <strong>Collect the sentences, not just the certificate.</strong>},
q{每门合规课程都写着<strong>银行面向监管者的英语</strong>——而那个语域正是你未来的邮件、工单、审计要用的。<strong>收集句子，而不只是收集证书。</strong>},
