dialogue => [
['Marco (Buddy)', q{Compliance week! <strong>My one piece of advice:</strong> do not speed-click. <em>Two of these modules are written better than our own docs</em> — and the language inside is the language of every audit you will ever face.}, q{合规周！<strong>我唯一建议：</strong>别狂点快进。<em>其中两门课写得比我们自己的文档还好</em>——里面的语言是你将来每次审计都会用的语言。}],
['You (New Joiner)', q{Reframing it as domain education then. <strong>Module one, data privacy — collecting sentences:</strong> <em>"personal data must be processed lawfully and transparently"</em> — <strong>that is modal-verb English</strong>: must, shall, may. <em>Every rule in this bank is graded by its modal.</em>}, q{那就把它重构为领域教育。<strong>模块一，数据隐私——收集句子：</strong><em>"personal data must be processed lawfully and transparently"</em>——<strong>这是情态动词英语</strong>：must、shall、may。<em>这家银行的每条规则都按它的情态动词分级。</em>}],
['Marco (Buddy)', q{Go on — <strong>you have discovered the modal ladder.</strong> <em>Must = regulator will punish. Shall = policy requires. Should = good practice. May = permitted, not promised.</em> Reading compliance text is reading modals with consequences.}, q{继续——<strong>你发现了情态动词阶梯。</strong><em>Must = 监管会处罚。Shall = 政策强制。Should = 最佳实践。May = 允许但不承诺。</em>读合规文本就是读带后果的情态动词。}],
['You (New Joiner)', q{Then the practical question: <strong>when a client asks me for data, which modal applies to me?</strong> The module says <em>"personal data may only be shared where there is a lawful basis"</em> — <strong>so my English should be:</strong> <em>"I can share this once we have a lawful basis on record — the form takes two minutes, and I can start it now."</em>}, q{那么实操问题：<strong>客户向我要数据时，哪个情态动词适用于我？</strong>课程说 <em>"personal data may only be shared where there is a lawful basis"</em>——<strong>所以我的英语应该是：</strong><em>"有合法依据记录在案后我才能共享——表格只要两分钟，我现在就可以帮你启动。"</em>}],
['Marco (Buddy)', q{<strong>That sentence is exactly the register.</strong> Notice what it does: <em>it quotes the rule without lecturing</em>, it names the mechanism (lawful basis, form), and it ends with motion. <strong>Compliance English at its best is helpfulness with citations.</strong>}, q{<strong>这句话正是那个语域。</strong>注意它做了什么：<em>引用规则但不说教</em>、点明机制（合法依据、表格）、以行动收尾。<strong>最好的合规英语是"带出处的乐于助人"。</strong>}],
['You (New Joiner)', q{Module five, anti-bribery — <strong>the sentence everyone needs:</strong> <em>"gifts and hospitality must be declined where they could influence, or appear to influence, business decisions."</em> <strong>The operative word is "appear"</strong> — <em>the appearance test is stricter than the reality test.</em>}, q{模块五，反贿赂——<strong>人人需要的那句：</strong><em>"gifts and hospitality must be declined where they could influence, or appear to influence, business decisions."</em><strong>关键词是 "appear"</strong>——<em>观感测试比事实测试更严格。</em>}],
['Marco (Buddy)', q{<strong>And that is the sentence you will actually use</strong> — the vendor who offers the nice dinner. <em>"I appreciate it — but anything that could appear to influence a decision has to go through the gifts register, and honestly, dinner does not clear that bar."</em> <strong>Same warmth, new citation.</strong>}, q{<strong>而这就是你真会用到的句子</strong>——那个请你吃大餐的供应商。<em>"我很感激——但任何可能 'appear to influence' 决定的东西都要走礼品登记，说实话，这顿饭过不了那个线。"</strong><em>同样的温度，新的出处。</em>}],
['You (New Joiner)', q{Twelve hours later, three certificates and <strong>a sentence bank</strong>: the modal ladder, the lawful-basis reply, the appearance test. <strong>The toll booth was a phrasebook.</strong>}, q{12 小时后，三张证书和<strong>一个句子库</strong>：情态阶梯、合法依据回复、观感测试。<strong>收费站原来是常用语手册。</strong>}],
