q{第 32 天。你的仪表盘走查收获热烈表扬——<em>"很棒，非常清晰"</em>——来自三个人。<strong>而你一无所获。</strong>温暖令人愉快；具体才是燃料。<strong>夸奖与反馈的区别在于：你能不能在周五前对它采取行动。</strong>},
q{The craft: <strong>mine the compliment for its specifics</strong> — the situation-action-effect probe turns "great job" into <em>"when you paused at the risk slide, that landed"</em>, which converts into <em>a habit you can repeat</em>. And the mirror question — <strong>"what would you cut?"</strong> — is where the real gold hides.},
q{手艺：<strong>从夸奖里挖具体性</strong>——情境-行动-效果探针把"很棒"变成<em>"你在风险页暂停的那一刻很有效"</em>，进而转化为<em>可以重复的习惯</em>。而镜像问题——<strong>"你会砍掉什么？"</strong>——才是真金所在。},
],
dialogue => [
['Priya (Delivery)', q{Great walkthrough yesterday — <em>really clear.</em>}, q{昨天的走查很棒——<em>非常清晰。</em>}],
['You (New Joiner)', q{Thank you — <strong>and can I mine it for one minute?</strong> <em>Clear how — which moment specifically did the job?</em> I am collecting what works so I can repeat it on purpose.}, q{谢谢——<strong>我能花一分钟挖一下吗？</strong><em>哪里清晰——具体哪个瞬间起了作用？</em>我在收集"有效"，好让我可以刻意重复。}],
['Priya (Delivery)', q{Huh — nobody asks the follow-up. <strong>Two moments:</strong> when you paused on the risk slide and said <em>"correct today, breaks when X"</em> — <em>the room stopped scrolling and started thinking.</em> And your one-sentence summary at the end — <em>three decisions, three owners, one date.</em>}, q{咦——没人会问后续。<strong>两个瞬间：</strong>你在风险页停顿并说出 <em>"今天是对的、X 时会坏"</em>——<em>整个房间停止了滑动、开始思考。</em>还有结尾的一句话总结——<em>三个决定、三个责任人、一个日期。</em>}],
['You (New Joiner)', q{That is gold — <strong>situation, action, effect, and now I can repeat both on purpose.</strong> The pause was deliberate; <em>I will keep it as a rule.</em> Now the mirror question — <strong>if you were running that walkthrough, what would you have cut?</strong>}, q{这是金子——<strong>情境、行动、效果，现在我可以刻意重复两者了。</strong>停顿是刻意的；<em>我会把它保留为规则。</em>现在是镜像问题——<strong>如果是你来讲，你会砍掉什么？</strong>}],
['Priya (Delivery)', q{Slide four — the methodology appendix. <strong>Half the room was lost and the half that cared can read.</strong> <em>Link it, name it, move on.</em> And one more, since you asked: <strong>you apologised twice for being new</strong> — <em>the content did not need the disclaimer.</em>}, q{第四页——方法论附录。<strong>一半的人跟不上，另一半在乎的人自己会读。</strong><em>链接它、命名它、继续走。</em>再送一条，既然你问了：<strong>你为"自己是新人"道歉了两次</strong>——<em>内容不需要免责声明。</em>}],
['You (New Joiner)', q{Both sting productively. <strong>So the working list:</strong> keep the risk-slide pause, keep the triple-summary, <em>link-and-name the appendices</em>, and <strong>retire the "as a new joiner" disclaimer</strong> — <em>the work is the credential.</em> That is four actions I can start Friday.}, q{两条都刺得有效。<strong>所以工作清单：</strong>保留风险页停顿、保留三句式总结、<em>附录改为链接加命名</em>、<strong>退役"作为新人"的免责声明</strong>——<em>作品本身就是资质。</em>这就是周五就能启动的四个动作。}],
['Elena (Tech Lead)', q{Overheard — <strong>you just ran the best feedback conversation I have seen this quarter.</strong> <em>Nobody mines praise;</em> they archive it like a trophy. <strong>You treated it as raw ore.</strong>}, q{都听到了——<strong>你刚刚完成了本季度我见过最好的一次反馈对话。</strong><em>没人去挖夸奖；</em>他们把它像奖杯一样归档。<strong>你把它当原矿处理。</strong>}],
['You (New Joiner)', q{Because <strong>a compliment I cannot act on is just weather</strong> — pleasant, gone by Friday. <em>Mined, it is a habit with a name.</em> <strong>Same probe next time someone says "great job" — and I owe Priya a walk-through of slide-four surgery.</strong>}, q{因为<strong>无法行动的夸奖只是天气</strong>——宜人、周五就散。<em>挖开，它就是一个有名字的习惯。</em><strong>下次有人说"很棒"还是用这个探针——我还欠 Priya 一场第四页的手术演示。</strong>}],
