grammar => [
['The trade frame: "what do you want in return?"', q{<em>"You emailed me a routing map? … What do you want in return?"</em> — the moment Priya names the trade, the value-first method has already won: your artifact converted a cold approach into a negotiation. Answer with sized asks, never "nothing" — <em>"nothing" refunds the value and ends the trade.</em>}, q{"You emailed me a routing map? … What do you want in return?"——当 Priya 点名这笔交易时，价值先行法已经赢了：你的产物把冷启动变成了谈判。用有尺寸的请求回答，绝不说"没什么"——<em>"没什么"等于退款，交易结束。</em>}],
['Promissory futures in follow-ups', q{<em>"Alert list draft by Friday as promised."</em>, <em>"Next time something in my lane reaches your team, I will send it with context."</em> — follow-up grammar is <strong>[delivered] + [promised] + [future protocol]</strong>. The trace does triple duty: gratitude, accountability, and a standing rule for the relationship. One email, three deposits.}, q{"Alert list draft by Friday as promised."、"Next time something in my lane reaches your team, I will send it with context."——跟进语法是<strong>[已交付] + [已承诺] + [未来协议]</strong>。痕迹一份邮件三重存款：致谢、问责、关系准则。}],
],
tips => [
q{<strong>Value first, always.</strong> A routing map beats a complaint email — and gets praised to your manager, unsolicited.},
q{<strong>Every coffee leaves a trace.</strong> Same-day, one line: took, promised, when. The trace is what makes a relationship compound.},
q{<strong>When asked "what do you want in return?", have a real answer.</strong> Two small asks — learning time and a name — beat one false "nothing".},
q{<strong>The ledger is a memory, not a score.</strong> Repay visibly where it lands best: a doc credit, a context-first handoff, a shipped alert.},
q{<strong>The no-surprise promise is network currency.</strong> "I will send it with context" is why residents start routing things to you.},
],
practice => [
